        "text": "The term DEFI was created in 2018 by several Ethereum developers, but the actual defi movement arguably started with the creation of Bitcoin in 2009. Bitcoin could be considered the first peer to peer digital money built on blockchain technology, which can be classified as DeFi. The real milestone in Defi, however, is the launch of the ethereum network. In 2015, Ethereum introduced smart Contracts, a more versatile programming language, and the ERC 20 token standards. The protocol supports smart contracts that provide functions suitable for financial services, such as decentralized asset lending. The Ethereum network quickly began attracting developers to build all kinds of DApps, making Ethereum the foundation for Defi applications. The Defi space experienced exceptional growth after that.",
